; DOMAIN: symmetric-monoidal-infinity-category [CLOSED, derived 2026-07-24]
; Claim: A symmetric monoidal infinity-category is a coCartesian fibration C^otimes -> Fin_* (Segal's category of pointed finite sets) such that the Segal maps C^otimes_{<n>} -> (C^otimes_{<1>})^n are equivalences; equivalently an E_infinity-monoid (commutative algebra) object in the infinity-category Cat_infinity. The fiber over <1> is the underlying category C, and the active map <2>->{<1> gives the tensor bifunctor otimes: C x C -> C, coherently associative and commutative up to all higher homotopies encoded by the E_infinity operad. Commutative algebra objects CAlg(C) = sections of C^otimes -> Fin_* preserving inert maps = E_infinity-algebras in C; when C=Sp this recovers E_infinity-ring spectra. On presentable categories, Day convolution equips Fun(C,D) with a symmetric monoidal structure when C is symmetric monoidal and D is presentable sym-mon, left Kan extending otimes; the Lurie tensor product on Pr^L is itself the universal such structure with unit Spaces. E_infinity = colimit of the operadic tower over E_n (Boardman-Vogt), the infinite little-cubes/Barratt-Eccles operad.
; Bridge: genesis_presentable_category (the Lurie tensor product makes Pr^L symmetric monoidal; CAlg(Pr^L) = presentable symmetric monoidal infinity-categories, and Day convolution builds sym-mon structures on presentable functor categories) + genesis_infinity_category (a symmetric monoidal infinity-category is an E_infinity-algebra object IN Cat_infinity via a coCartesian fibration over Fin_*; the Segal condition is an infinity-categorical limit statement) + genesis_stable_infinity_category (Sp is symmetric monoidal under smash with unit S; CAlg(Sp)=E_infinity-ring spectra, and stable presentable sym-mon cats are modules over Sp).
(= (symmetric-monoidal-category $C) (E-infinity-monoid $C Cat-infinity))
(= (E-infinity-monoid $C $K) (cocartesian-fibration-over $C Fin-pointed))
(= (segal-condition $C) (equivalence (fiber $C <n>) (power (fiber $C <1>) $n)))
(= (tensor-product $C) (active-map-<2>-to-<1> $C))
(= (CAlg $C) (E-infinity-algebras-in $C))
(= (CAlg Spectra) (E-infinity-ring-spectra))
(= (day-convolution $C $D) (left-kan-extension-of tensor (functor-category $C $D)))
(= (unit (lurie-tensor-PrL)) Spaces)